  "helpConnectTitle": "Connecting",
  "helpConnectBody": "Pick a port, set the baud rate and press Connect. The port list refreshes every 2 seconds, so plugging or unplugging a cable shows up right away. On connect, Portside sends one Enter to wake up the prompt.",
  "helpTabsTitle": "Tabs",
  "helpTabsBody": "Open a new session (tab) with + to talk to several ports at once. Background tabs keep receiving and logging data. The last tab can't be closed.",
  "helpTypingTitle": "Typing in the Terminal",
  "helpTypingBody": "Click the terminal to focus it and type. Arrow keys, Ctrl combinations and Backspace all work. On macOS, Korean input composition breaks because of a library limitation.",
  "helpSenderTitle": "Line Sender",
  "helpSenderBody": "Write several lines ahead of time and press Enter to send only the line with the cursor. Ctrl+Enter inserts a new line. After sending, the cursor moves to the end of the next line, so pressing Enter repeatedly sends the lines in order.",
  "helpHexTitle": "Hex View",
  "helpHexBody": "Switch with the Terminal/Hex toggle in the toolbar. It shows the bytes actually received as a hex dump.",
  "helpLoggingTitle": "Logging",
  "helpLoggingBody": "Press the ● button (or {shortcut}) to choose where to save the log. Several tabs can log at the same time.",
  "helpSettingsTitle": "Font / Color Scheme",
  "helpSettingsBody": "Change the font, size, terminal color scheme (Solarized, Dracula, Nord, Gruvbox and more) and scrollback length in Settings (⚙). They are kept across restarts. The app's light/dark mode and language are in the buttons at the right of the tab bar.",
